<title>SRI LANKA: Korea Ceylon up 15 pct, volume thin.</title>
<headline>Korea Ceylon up 15 pct, volume thin.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Korea Ceylon Footwear Manufacturing Co Ltd shares rose 15 percent, or 1.50 rupees, to 11.50 on limited buying by small-scale investors, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The share is relatively illiquid and the price rises on any slightest buying interest,&quot; said a retail broker.</p>
<p>Small investors are attracted to the stock because of its low price, he said. The price rise was on a trade volume of only 4,000 shares.</p>
<p>--Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
